; S:Node-Resident-Regress - node.library / uv1.library expunge paths
; (aros-adt-src d3411393): a resident node.library must survive a library
; flush from a foreign task (vetoed, stays resident with LIBF_DELEXP) and
; expunge cleanly from its own last closer, and C:Node must reopen it after
; both.  CLI commands run in the shell's own process, so "Avail FLUSH" from
; this shell is the closer task and "Run Avail FLUSH" is a foreign one.
; Run: AROS_LAUNCH_VIA=shell AROS_SHELL_CMD='Execute S:Node-Resident-Regress'
;      AROS_ACTIONS_FILE=tests/actions/node-resident-regress.txt - Execute feeds
;      the script into the calling shell, so a redirect on Execute does not
;      capture the Echo lines: the resident-70 snapshot of the console is the
;      evidence (NODE1..4_RC=0 and NODE4_EVAL_OK)
Echo "NODE_RESIDENT_START"
Stack 10485760
C:Node --version
Echo "NODE1_RC=$RC"
Avail FLUSH >NIL:
Echo "FLUSH_SAME_TASK_DONE"
C:Node --version
Echo "NODE2_RC=$RC"
Run >NIL: Avail FLUSH
Wait 3
Echo "FLUSH_FOREIGN_TASK_DONE"
C:Node --version
Echo "NODE3_RC=$RC"
Run >NIL: Avail FLUSH
Wait 3
Avail FLUSH >NIL:
Echo "FLUSH_BOTH_DONE"
C:Node -e "console.log('NODE4_EVAL_OK ' + process.version)"
Echo "NODE4_RC=$RC"
Echo "NODE_RESIDENT_DONE"
Wait 5
